<title>GERMANY: Deutsche seeks suspension of Traub stock.</title>
<headline>Deutsche seeks suspension of Traub stock.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Traub AG of Germany said on Monday it faced serious liquidity problems and a meeting of its creditors would take place later in the day.</p>
<p>Lead creditor Deutsche Bank has requested that the company's stock be suspended from trading, Traub said in a regulatory news release.</p>
<p>Traub also said it would issue a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Stock in Traub, an engineering company, closed on Friday at 33 marks ($21.56), above a year-low of 30.50 marks and a high of 145 marks. ($ = 1.53 German Marks)</p>
</text>
